    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  Beyond algebraic functions, Further Mathematics requires differentiating <span class="learn-keyword">trigonometric</span>, <span class="learn-keyword">logarithmic</span>, and <span class="learn-keyword">exponential</span> functions &mdash; each with its own standard derivative that must be memorized and combined with the chain rule when needed.</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Standard Trigonometric Derivatives</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Function</th><th>Derivative</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>sin x</td><td>cos x</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>cos x</td><td>&minus;sin x</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>tan x</td><td>sec&sup2;x</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n<p class="learn-p"><strong>Example:</strong> Differentiate y = sin(3x) (chain rule): dy/dx = 3cos(3x).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Exponential Functions</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">If y = e&#8319;, dy/dx = e&#8319; (its own derivative &mdash; unique to base e). If y = e<sup>kx</sup>, dy/dx = ke<sup>kx</sup> (chain rule).<br>\n<strong>Example:</strong> y = e&#8309;&#8319; &rArr; dy/dx = 5e&#8309;&#8319;.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Logarithmic Functions</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">If y = ln x (natural log), dy/dx = 1/x. If y = ln(f(x)), dy/dx = f&prime;(x)/f(x) (chain rule).<br>\n<strong>Example:</strong> y = ln(2x + 1) &rArr; dy/dx = 2/(2x+1).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Combining with the Chain Rule</h3>\n<p class="learn-p"><strong>Example:</strong> Differentiate y = e<sup>x&sup2;</sup>. Outer: e<sup>(&middot;)</sup>, inner: x&sup2; (derivative 2x). dy/dx = 2x&middot;e<sup>x&sup2;</sup>.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">&#128161;</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Whenever the angle, exponent, or log argument is anything other than plain x, you MUST apply the chain rule and multiply by the derivative of that inner expression &mdash; forgetting this multiplier is the most common error in this topic.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">&#127919;</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> Memorize: d/dx(sin x)=cos x, d/dx(cos x)=&minus;sin x, d/dx(e&#8319;)=e&#8319;, d/dx(ln x)=1/x. Always apply the chain rule when the input is a function of x rather than plain x.\n</div>\n',
