    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  A <span class="learn-keyword">parabola</span> is the curve traced by a point that moves so that its distance from a fixed point (the <span class="learn-keyword">focus</span>) equals its distance from a fixed line (the <span class="learn-keyword">directrix</span>). Parabolas appear in projectile motion, satellite dishes, and bridge cables.</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Standard Equation</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">The simplest parabola with vertex at the origin, opening rightward: y&sup2; = 4ax, where a &gt; 0.<br>\nFocus: (a, 0). Directrix: x = &minus;a. Axis of symmetry: the x-axis.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Key Features</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Equation</th><th>Opens</th><th>Focus</th><th>Directrix</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>y&sup2; = 4ax</td><td>Right</td><td>(a, 0)</td><td>x = &minus;a</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>y&sup2; = &minus;4ax</td><td>Left</td><td>(&minus;a, 0)</td><td>x = a</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>x&sup2; = 4ay</td><td>Up</td><td>(0, a)</td><td>y = &minus;a</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>x&sup2; = &minus;4ay</td><td>Down</td><td>(0, &minus;a)</td><td>y = a</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Worked Example</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Find the focus and directrix of y&sup2; = 12x.<br>\nComparing to y&sup2;=4ax: 4a=12 &rArr; a=3. Focus = (3, 0). Directrix: x = &minus;3.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. The Parabola as a Locus</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Every point P(x, y) on the parabola satisfies: distance to focus = distance to directrix. This defining property can be used to derive the equation from scratch, and to verify whether a given point lies on the curve.</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">&#128161;</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> Always compare the given equation to the standard form y&sup2;=4ax (or x&sup2;=4ay) FIRST to identify \'a\' before stating the focus and directrix &mdash; don\'t just guess from the numbers.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">&#127919;</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> A parabola y&sup2;=4ax opens rightward with focus (a,0) and directrix x=&minus;a. Every point on the parabola is equidistant from the focus and directrix &mdash; this locus property defines the shape.\n</div>\n',
