    term: 'Second Term',
    contentHTML:
      '\n<div class="learn-intro">\n  A <span class="learn-keyword">hyperbola</span> is the locus of points where the DIFFERENCE of distances to two fixed foci is constant. Unlike the ellipse\'s closed loop, a hyperbola consists of two separate, open branches.</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">1. Standard Equation</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Centred at the origin, opening left-right: x&sup2;/a&sup2; &minus; y&sup2;/b&sup2; = 1.<br>\nVertices: (&plusmn;a, 0). Foci: (&plusmn;c, 0), where c&sup2; = a&sup2; + b&sup2; (note: PLUS, unlike the ellipse).</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">2. Key Features</h3>\n<div class="learn-table-wrap">\n  <table class="learn-table">\n    <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Formula</th></tr></thead>\n    <tbody>\n      <tr><td>Focal relationship</td><td>c&sup2; = a&sup2; + b&sup2;</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Eccentricity</td><td>e = c/a (always &gt; 1 for a hyperbola)</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Asymptotes</td><td>y = &plusmn;(b/a)x</td></tr>\n      <tr><td>Transverse axis</td><td>Length 2a, joins the two vertices</td></tr>\n    </tbody>\n  </table>\n</div>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">3. Worked Example</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">Find the foci, eccentricity, and asymptotes of x&sup2;/16 &minus; y&sup2;/9 = 1.<br>\na&sup2;=16 &rArr; a=4. b&sup2;=9 &rArr; b=3. c&sup2;=16+9=25 &rArr; c=5.<br>\nFoci: (&plusmn;5, 0). Eccentricity: e=c/a=5/4=1.25. Asymptotes: y = &plusmn;(3/4)x.</p>\n\n<h3 class="learn-subheading">4. Definition Check</h3>\n<p class="learn-p">For any point P on the hyperbola, |PF&#8321; &minus; PF&#8322;| = 2a (the absolute difference of distances to the two foci is constant).</p>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">&#128161;</span>\n  <strong>Exam Tip:</strong> The key difference from the ellipse: for a hyperbola, c&sup2; = a&sup2; + b&sup2; (addition, since c &gt; a always). For an ellipse, c&sup2; = a&sup2; &minus; b&sup2; (subtraction, since c &lt; a always). Mixing these up is the most common error between the two conics.\n</div>\n\n<div class="learn-tip-box">\n  <span class="learn-tip-icon">&#127919;</span>\n  <strong>Summary:</strong> x&sup2;/a&sup2;&minus;y&sup2;/b&sup2;=1 describes a hyperbola opening left-right, with foci (&plusmn;c,0) where c&sup2;=a&sup2;+b&sup2;, eccentricity always &gt;1, and asymptotes y=&plusmn;(b/a)x that the branches approach but never touch.\n</div>\n',
